    "verdict": "On the exercised APFS schedules and primitives, no tested primitive enforced an atomic expected-version precondition for an existing note against an independent external writer. A final reread detected an external write that landed before it, but a second write landing after the reread was lost; content/mtime ABA was indistinguishable in the exercised schedules. This is not a universal impossibility claim: cloud and network backends and other filesystems were not tested, and the ETag row is a local model, not provider evidence. Descriptor-relative traversal contained a root swap but did not bind the visible root. O_EXCL held for concurrent new-name namespace no-clobber only; it makes no crash-safe or complete-creation claim. Keep automatic and engine-applied reviewed replacement for existing notes on ordinary folders disabled and retain the proposed diff for manual application."
  },
